From fdbf05ded7d35a19ab59091137eac48e18cbf8c9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: forge-shepherd <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 10 Jul 2026 17:07:37 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] feat(shepherd): add --pull to extract failure excerpts +
 review-thread fix-list

forge shepherd <pr> --pull returns ONE compact payload an agent can act on
without running gh pr checks / gh run view --log-failed / GraphQL by hand:

- failures[]: per FAILED check {name, conclusion, jobUrl, excerpt, alsoFailedOn}.
  excerpt = the actual (fail)/assertion/error lines pulled from the job log
  (not the whole log), capped ~30 lines. Identical excerpts across matrix jobs
  collapse to ONE entry with alsoFailedOn = count of the other jobs.
- reviewThreads[]: unresolved, non-outdated threads needing action, INCLUDING
  review bots (CodeRabbit et al.) since those comments are the fixes; excludes
  resolved/outdated/self/pure-automation. {file,line,author,body,threadId,commentId}.
- decision state + one-line summary from the existing pass (unchanged).

All gh I/O goes through an injected runGh runner so unit tests use fixtures,
never live GitHub. Token caps bound the payload (10 failures / 20 threads /
30 excerpt lines). Adapter additively surfaces comment fullDatabaseId as
commentId for replies. runShepherdPass state machine is untouched.

Refs: 33e1bbd3-ca82-4246-86ff-d1d18717dd9b

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
